# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ARC Stay — environment template
# Copy to .env (`cp .env.example .env`) and fill in. NEVER commit .env.
# The POC runs end to end with ONLY the two DATABASE_* values below set.
# Every integration is optional and falls back to a deterministic mock.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Required ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Every environment sets this. The one exception is a managed Postgres attached
# through a hosting provider's storage integration, which may write the
# connection string under a prefixed name such as MYPREFIX_DATABASE_URL; that is
# picked up automatically. See src/lib/database-url.ts.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://arc:arc@127.0.0.1:5432/arc_stay?schema=public"
# Separate database used by `npm run test:integration`. It is reset on each run.
TEST_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://arc:arc@127.0.0.1:5432/arc_stay_test?schema=public"

# --- Secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Each any string >= 32 chars. Development defaults are used when unset so the
# POC boots with no configuration; ALWAYS set both explicitly outside
# development, and keep them DIFFERENT from each other — reusing the session
# key as the analytics salt would let anyone who can read the analytics table
# test guesses against the key that signs sessions.
AUTH_SECRET=""
ANALYTICS_SALT=""

# --- Hosted demo front door (optional) --------------------------------------
# Shared passphrase for a hosted walkthrough. Unset (the default) means no
# gate, which is what local development and the test suites want. When set,
# every route redirects to /gate until the passphrase is entered. It locks the
# front door only: the demo sign-in behind it still hands out a session with no
# credential, and every role and tenant check still re-derives from the
# database. Requires AUTH_SECRET, which keys the cookie. Compared trimmed and
# case-folded, so a phone keyboard's capital letter does not lock anyone out.
ARC_DEMO_PASSPHRASE=""

# Say out loud that this deployment's demo is open to anyone with the URL.
#
# Needed only in production, and only while ARC_DATA_MODE=demo, where the
# sign-in page issues an owner session with no credential. Set this OR
# ARC_DEMO_PASSPHRASE; a production demo that sets neither refuses to start,
# because "open to the internet" should be a decision rather than an omission.
ARC_ALLOW_OPEN_DEMO=""

# Keys the seeded guests' portal tokens (src/lib/demo-portals.ts).
#
# A portal token is a bearer credential: whoever holds one can change that
# guest's preferences, basket and bookings. The seed's tokens used to be
# literals in the repository. Leave this empty locally — there is a documented
# non-secret fallback so a clean checkout works — and set 32+ random characters
# in production, which refuses to start without it.
#   openssl rand -hex 32
ARC_SEED_TOKEN_SECRET=""

# Bearer token for the detailed form of GET /api/health, for an uptime checker.
#
# Unset means the detailed form is unavailable, never that it is open. The
# anonymous form always answers, with status and the time and nothing else.
MONITORING_TOKEN=""

# --- Demo / safety switches -------------------------------------------------
# "demo" labels all money and metrics as synthetic and blocks live payments.
ARC_DATA_MODE="demo"
# Hard kill switch for outbound guest messaging. Never enable in the POC.
ARC_ENABLE_OUTBOUND_MESSAGING="false"

# --- AI provider (optional) -------------------------------------------------
# "mock" (default) = deterministic fixtures, zero network, zero cost.
# "anthropic" = live provider; requires ANTHROPIC_API_KEY.
AI_PROVIDER="mock"
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=""
AI_MODEL="claude-sonnet-5-5"
AI_MAX_TOKENS="2048"
# Per-user AI calls allowed per rolling minute.
AI_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE="10"

# --- Payments (optional, MVP) -----------------------------------------------
# "simulated" (default) = no network, no charges. Live keys are refused while
# ARC_DATA_MODE=demo. "stripe" requires BOTH values below: without the webhook
# secret, a payment that later failed could never release its capacity, so the
# app refuses to start rather than run half-configured. See ADR-026.
PAYMENTS_PROVIDER="simulated"
# Starts "sk_". Never sent to a browser.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=""
# Stripe's signing secret for POST /api/webhooks/stripe (starts "whsec_").
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""
# Starts "pk_". This one IS sent to the browser — it is what Stripe.js
# initialises with, and without it the guest has no way to pay: the Payment
# Element cannot load and checkout refuses every order for want of a confirmed
# payment. Checked for the "pk_" prefix at startup, because a secret key pasted
# into this slot would be published.
STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=""

# --- Integration providers --------------------------------------------------
# Each of the four below has exactly ONE accepted value, because exactly one
# implementation exists. They used to accept mapbox, google, stormglass,
# openweather, twilio, resend and posthog, with nothing behind any of them:
# setting one changed what /admin/health printed and changed no behaviour.
# CONDITIONS_PROVIDER=stormglass was the dangerous one — it told an operator
# live marine data was feeding the conditions gate while the gate carried on
# reading seeded ConditionReport rows. Those names are now refused at startup
# with a message saying so, and their API-key variables warn that they are not
# read. Adding a value back without an implementation is a type error.

# "fixture" = the seeded travel-time matrix for Puerto Escondido (ADR-011).
MAPS_PROVIDER="fixture"

# "fixture" = seeded seven-day conditions, which is what the safety gate in
# modules/destination/conditions reads. Readings are ALWAYS rendered with a
# freshness timestamp and never as a safety guarantee.
CONDITIONS_PROVIDER="fixture"

# --- Travel advice / culture context (optional) -----------------------------
# "fixture" (default) = a GOV.UK-shaped demo payload in the repository, offline.
# "govuk" = the live GOV.UK Content API (no key). Refused while
# ARC_DATA_MODE=demo. Output is always labelled advisory, never law.
TRAVEL_ADVICE_PROVIDER="fixture"

# "noop" = refuses to deliver. Outbound guest messaging is a kill switch
# (ARC_ENABLE_OUTBOUND_MESSAGING), not a provider choice: non-negotiable 6.
#
# This is NOT the setting for confirmations, invitations or password resets.
# Those are transactional mail and have their own section below. See ADR-040.
MESSAGING_PROVIDER="noop"

# --- Transactional email ----------------------------------------------------
# A different permission from the kill switch above, deliberately. That one is
# about ARC *initiating* contact with a guest and stays off. This one is about
# the reply to something a named person just did: the invitation an owner
# pressed "invite" to send, the confirmation of a booking a guest just paid
# for, the reset of a password somebody just asked to reset. ADR-040.
#
# Off by default: a deployment that says nothing sends nothing.
ARC_ENABLE_TRANSACTIONAL_EMAIL="false"

# Where this deployment is reached, no trailing slash. REQUIRED once the switch
# above is on, because every message carries a link — and ARC will not take the
# origin from a request header, which would let whoever sent the request choose
# where the recipient's credential-bearing link pointed.
#
# Worth setting even with delivery off: with it set, MAIL_PROVIDER="log"
# records complete messages with their real links, which is what /owner/messages
# shows and the only way to read the copy before a guest does.
ARC_PUBLIC_URL=""

# "log"    = record the message in full and deliver nothing. The default, and
#            an honest mode rather than a stub: status LOGGED, never SENT.
# "resend" = POST to the Resend API. Requires RESEND_API_KEY and ARC_MAIL_FROM,
#            and is REFUSED while ARC_DATA_MODE=demo with the demo open — the
#            demo sign-in issues an owner session with no credential, and an
#            owner can invite a partner at any address, so a live provider
#            there is an open relay sending from ARC's own domain.
MAIL_PROVIDER="log"
RESEND_API_KEY=""
# On a domain verified with Resend. Mail from an unverified domain is accepted
# by the API and then not delivered, which is the failure nobody notices.
ARC_MAIL_FROM=""
# Optional. Unset means replies go to ARC_MAIL_FROM.
ARC_MAIL_REPLY_TO="

# --- Observability (optional, MVP) ------------------------------------------
# "internal" = persisted to AnalyticsEvent and forwarded nowhere.
ANALYTICS_PROVIDER="internal"
# Unset: faults go to stderr. Set: faults are reported to Sentry's envelope
# endpoint. A 4xx AppError is never reported either way. See docs/operations.md.
SENTRY_DSN=""

# --- Scheduled jobs (optional) ----------------------------------------------
# Shared secret for the routes under /api/cron. UNSET MEANS THOSE ROUTES 404 —
# never "no authorisation required". vercel.json schedules the hold sweep, the
# invariant check and the mail dispatcher.
CRON_SECRET=""
